{
  "id": "parabolas-u2",
  "title": "Unit 2",
  "subtitle": "Forgiveness and Grace",
  "guide": {
    "summary": "Jesus revealed the depth of God's grace through parables about forgiveness. He showed that God forgives infinitely, celebrates the return of sinners, and invites the hardened heart to surrender to his immeasurable love.",
    "keyVerses": [
      {
        "reference": "Luke 15:20-24",
        "text": "He arose, and came to his father. But while he was still far off, his father saw him, and was moved with compassion, and ran, and fell on his neck, and kissed him. The son said to him, 'Father, I have sinned against heaven, and in your sight. I am no more worthy to be called your son.' But the father said to his servants, 'Bring out the best robe, and put it on him. Put a ring on his hand, and shoes on his feet.'"
      },
      {
        "reference": "Luke 15:32",
        "text": "It was appropriate to celebrate and be glad, for this your brother was dead, and is alive again. He was lost, and is found."
      },
      {
        "reference": "Matthew 18:21-22",
        "text": "Then Peter came and said to him, 'Lord, how often shall my brother sin against me, and I forgive him? Until seven times?' Jesus said to him, 'I don't tell you until seven times, but until seventy times seven.'"
      }
    ]
  },
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "parabolas-u2-l1",
      "title": "The Prodigal Son",
      "icon": "heart.fill",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e1",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "What did the prodigal son ask his father?",
          "text": "\"Father, give me my share of the ___\".",
          "speaker": "Prodigal son",
          "options": [
            "inheritance",
            "house",
            "property",
            "wealth"
          ],
          "answer": "inheritance",
          "reference": "Luke 15:12"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e2",
          "kind": "typeAnswer",
          "prompt": "Type the missing word",
          "text": "The prodigal son went to live in a ___ country and lost everything.",
          "answer": "distant",
          "options": [
            "distant",
            "faraway",
            "remote",
            "foreign"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 15:13"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e3",
          "kind": "buildVerse",
          "prompt": "Build the verse of decision",
          "text": "When the son returns",
          "tokens": [
            "Rising up",
            "went to",
            "his father"
          ],
          "distractors": [
            "left the road",
            "ran away",
            "went ahead",
            "departed far"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 15:20"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e4",
          "kind": "orderEvents",
          "prompt": "Put the story in order",
          "text": "Sequence of the Parable of the Prodigal Son.",
          "tokens": [
            "Son asks for inheritance",
            "Squanders it in vice",
            "Returns in repentance",
            "Father celebrates his return"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 15:11-32"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e5",
          "kind": "matchPairs",
          "prompt": "Match the elements",
          "pairs": [
            {
              "left": "Prodigal son",
              "right": "Returns in repentance"
            },
            {
              "left": "Loving father",
              "right": "Receives with grace"
            },
            {
              "left": "Older son",
              "right": "Resentment"
            },
            {
              "left": "Feast",
              "right": "Celebration of forgiveness"
            }
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 15:11-32"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e6",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "The father rejected the prodigal son because of his sins.",
          "isTrue": false,
          "reference": "Luke 15:20-24",
          "explanation": "The father ran to meet him, kissed him, and celebrated his return with a great feast."
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e7",
          "kind": "listen",
          "prompt": "What did the father do?",
          "text": "Listen: The father celebrated the son's return with joy.",
          "options": [
            "Celebrated with joy",
            "Rejected the son",
            "Demanded explanations",
            "Apologized"
          ],
          "answer": "Celebrated with joy",
          "reference": "Luke 15:23-24"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l1-e8",
          "kind": "speak",
          "prompt": "Read aloud",
          "text": "This my son was dead, and is alive again.",
          "reference": "Luke 15:24"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parabolas-u2-l2",
      "title": "The Lost Sheep",
      "icon": "leaf.fill",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e1",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "How many sheep did the shepherd leave?",
          "text": "The shepherd left ___ sheep to look for the lost one.",
          "options": [
            "ninety-nine",
            "one hundred",
            "ninety",
            "eighty"
          ],
          "answer": "ninety-nine",
          "reference": "Luke 15:4"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e2",
          "kind": "typeAnswer",
          "prompt": "Type the missing word",
          "text": "\"If he finds it, he rejoices over it more than over the ninety ___\".",
          "answer": "nine",
          "options": [
            "nine",
            "nine that",
            "that didn't get lost",
            "remaining"
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 18:13"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e3",
          "kind": "buildVerse",
          "prompt": "Build the verse",
          "text": "The joy of the shepherd when finding",
          "tokens": [
            "There is more joy",
            "in heaven",
            "over one sinner",
            "who repents"
          ],
          "distractors": [
            "over the sheep found",
            "in the fields",
            "among men",
            "forever"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 15:7"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e4",
          "kind": "orderEvents",
          "prompt": "Put the search in order",
          "text": "Sequence of the Lost Sheep.",
          "tokens": [
            "Shepherd notices one missing",
            "Leaves the ninety-nine",
            "Searches until he finds",
            "Carries it on his shoulders"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 15:4-6"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e5",
          "kind": "matchPairs",
          "prompt": "Match the meanings",
          "pairs": [
            {
              "left": "Shepherd",
              "right": "God seeking"
            },
            {
              "left": "Lost sheep",
              "right": "Sinner far away"
            },
            {
              "left": "Diligent search",
              "right": "Active grace"
            },
            {
              "left": "Heavenly joy",
              "right": "Repentance"
            }
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 15:3-7"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e6",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "The shepherd was happy only because he found the lost sheep.",
          "isTrue": false,
          "reference": "Luke 15:6-7",
          "explanation": "There was special joy in heaven among the angels when the sheep repented, not just from finding it."
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e7",
          "kind": "listen",
          "prompt": "What did the shepherd do?",
          "text": "Listen: The shepherd searches for the sheep until he finds it.",
          "options": [
            "Searches until he finds it",
            "Waits for it to return",
            "Forgets about it",
            "Sells it"
          ],
          "answer": "Searches until he finds it",
          "reference": "Luke 15:4"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u2-l2-e8",
          "kind": "speak",
          "prompt": "Read aloud",
          "text": "There is joy in heaven when one sinner repents.",
          "reference": "Luke 15:7"
        }
      ]
    },
